<title>HUNGARY: FORECAST-HUNGARY T-BILL, BOND YIELDS SEEN MIXED.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-HUNGARY T-BILL, BOND YIELDS SEEN MIXED.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Expectations of falling Hungarian inflation will boost demand for longer-term papers and limit it for shorter maturities at this week's government paper auctions, dealers said.</p>
<p>As a result, t-bill yields are likely to be stable or increase slightly while the two-year bond's yields will fall despite a high volume on offer, they said.</p>
<p>The dealers were mixed on the prospects of the new five-year fixed rate bond, adding that while the market is very interested in five-year lengths, the 17.5 percent maximum allowable yield might be too low to attract most investors.  SECURITIES     ONE-MONTH   THREE-MONTH   2YR-BOND  5YR-FIX,15%</p>
